::  name       receipt offer field count
::  shape      fields - int (@u32)
::  invariant  a ReceiptOfferFact carries exactly fifteen fields (schema -
::             receipt_id - holder_id - recipient_id - product_id -
::             product_digest - purpose - value_amount - value_unit -
::             value_basis - return_kind - issued_at - expires_at -
::             signer_id - signature)
::  example    15
::  readers    Mantra - Glow Tend - Sur museum - Patchouli weave
::  nib        equinox-e209-mantra-tend-v0
::
::  Equinox e209 - Mantra M7 -- seventh Mantra structure pedestal in src/shape/.
::  Names ReceiptOfferFact's field count from mantra/src/receipt_offer.rye,
::  the fact one admitted receipt offer publishes: who holds it, who receives
::  it, what it is for, what it is worth, when it was issued, when it expires,
::  and who signed it. Pedestal only; Rye still owns fact_refusal, fact_eql,
::  and the admission Log.
::
::  Fifteen SITS AT rune_shape.max_fields (15), rather than under it -- this is
::  the widest fact this room has named. A sixteenth field here would refuse
::  at the rune's own ceiling; `offer_fact_fields`'s own comptime assert in
::  mantra/src/receipt_offer.rye already stops the Rye from compiling if its
::  struct and its stated count ever disagree.
+$  receipt-offer-field-count-shape
  $:  fields=@u32
  ==
